sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Caller as CLI / REPL / Tests
    participant API as Thin frontend facade
    participant Reader as reader.rs
    participant Mod as module_extract.rs
    participant Macro as macro pipeline facade
    participant SexpKit as Shared synthetic Sexp builders
    participant Classifier as Shared top-level classifier
    participant Top as ast/top_level.rs
    participant Expr as ast/expr.rs
    participant Types as ast/types.rs + ast/patterns.rs
    participant Docs as Frontend CLAUDE.md / design notes

    Caller->>API: parse / expand / build request
    API->>Reader: source -> Vec<Sexp>
    API->>Docs: consult documented frontend invariants

    opt module forms present
        API->>Mod: extract declarations
        Note over Mod: Boundary contract is documented, and super is normalized here.
    end

    opt macro-related forms present
        API->>Macro: expand quasiquote / parse defmacro
        Macro->>SexpKit: canonical constructors + match/list helpers
    end

    alt batch program
        API->>Classifier: classify top-level form once
        Classifier->>Top: build declaration form
    else REPL input
        API->>Classifier: classify top-level form once
        Classifier->>Top: build declaration form when applicable
        Classifier->>Expr: otherwise build expression form
    end

    Top->>Types: shared annotation + type parsing
    Expr->>Types: shared annotation + pattern parsing

    Note right of Classifier: One dispatch path serves both batch and REPL entry.
    Note right of Top: ast_builder is split by subsystem, with smaller files and clearer ownership.
    Note right of SexpKit: Canonical synthetic Sexp helpers reduce hidden coupling and agent traps.
